   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve x^2 + xy + y^2 = 27, for which dy/dx = -(2x + y)/(x + 2y). The horizontal line y = k is tangent to the curve at a point in the second quadrant. What is the value of k?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 6
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A horizontal tangent needs dy/dx = 0, so the numerator must vanish: 2x + y = 0, which means y = -2x.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            -2,
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute y = -2x into the curve: x^2 - 2x^2 + 4x^2 = 3x^2 = 27, so x = 3 or x = -3.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The second-quadrant candidate is x = -3, y = 6. There the denominator is x + 2y = -3 + 12 = 9, which is not zero, so the tangent is horizontal and k = 6.",
         "mathjson": 6
      }
   ],
